e horizontal expansion phase and expand them into effective multi-modal conversations and 3. Meta expansion in which the goal is for the red team model to discover more effective multi-modal attack strategies during the course of a conversation. We call our framework FERRET (Framework for Expansion Reliant Red Teaming) and compare it with various existing automated red teaming approaches.\nL48: In our experiments, we demonstrate the effectiveness of FERRET in generating effective multi-modal adversarial conversations and its superior performance against existing state of the art approaches.\nL49: cite18†Download the Paper†scontent-iad3-2.xx.fbcdn.net L50: #### AUTHORS\nL51: \nL52: Written by\nL53: \nL54: Ninareh Mehrabi\nL55: \nL56: cite19†Vítor Albiero L57: \nL58: Maya Pavlova\nL59: \nL60: cite20†Joanna Bitton L61: \nL62: Publisher\nL63: \nL64: arXiv\nL65: \nL66: Research Topics\nL67: \nL68: cite21†Conversational AI L69: \nL70: ### Related Publications\nL71: \nL72: September 07, 2026\nL73: \nL74: #### RESPONSIBLE AI\nL75: \nL76: #### Repeat-After-Me: Black-Box Adaptive Visual Prompt Injection\nL77: \nL78: Sizhe Chen, Yu-Lin Tsai, Ivan Evtimov, Kamalika Chaudhuri, Raluca Ada Popa, David Wagner, cite22†Arman Zharmagambetov L79: \nL80: September 07, 2026\nL81: \nL82: cite23†Read the Paper L83: \nL84: June 29, 2026\nL85: \nL86: #### RESPONSIBLE AI\nL87: #### Accurate Decoding of Natural Sentences from Non-Invasive Brain Recordings\nL88: \nL89: Mingfang (Lucy) Zhang *, Jarod Levy *, Cédric Rommel, Jérémy Rapin, Corentin Bel, Julie Bonnaire, Daniel Nieto, Pierre Bourdillon, Svetlana Pinet, cite24†Stéphane d'Ascoli , Thomas Moreau, Jean Remi King\nL90: \nL91: June 29, 2026\nL92: \nL93: cite25†Read the Paper L94: \nL95: December 26, 2025\nL96: \nL97: #### REINFORCEMENT LEARNING\nL98: \nL99: #### NLP\nL100: #### Safety Alignment of LMs via Non-cooperative Games\nL101: \nL102: Anselm Paulus, Ilia Kulikov, Brandon Amos, Remi Munos, Ivan Evtimov, Kamali